  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63691,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 232,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>If extensive and/or architecturally complex, metaplasias may be associated with an underlying hyperplasia/carcinoma. These metaplasias include syncytial papillary change {22498936}, complex mucinous glandular proliferation {28232161}, morular metaplasia {19180120}, and complex papillary proliferation {23211295}. Papillary proliferation with striking mucinous metaplasia overlaps morphologically with papillary mucinous metaplasia (a precursor of mucinous carcinoma) {22766790; 29445890; 29449000}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T16:56:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
